#description: A schema in the text refers to the lineage's name, and the use also narrows the joinSchema with #J beside it. Only the schema's reference to name is refused; the narrowing's reference to #J is allowed.
#expect: E0141
#spec: docs/invariants.md:116-118, docs/invariants.md:162-165, docs/invariants.md:220
#at: lin.h

Both references a suite could refuse here are E0141, so #expect cannot tell
one finding from two. A suite that also refuses the narrowing's #J (#264)
gives the same verdict; its golden section shows the second finding.
-- in.cue --
import "github.com/sdboyer/thema"

#J: {[string]: string, ...}
lin: h: thema.Lineage & {name: "h", joinSchema: #J}
-- text.cue --
name: "h"
schemas: "0": "0": schema: {a?: string, n?: name}
-- out/fill-text-named/bind --
verdict: E0141
E0141 n in schema 0.0 refers to name, which is declared in the lineage outside the schema @ text.cue:2:45
-- out/fill-text/bind --
verdict: E0141
E0141 n in schema 0.0 refers to name, which is declared in the lineage outside the schema @ :2:45
-- out/fill-use/bind --
verdict: E0141
E0141 joinSchema refers to #J, which is declared in the lineage outside the joinSchema @ /m/in.cue:5:49
E0141 n in schema 0.0 refers to name, which is declared in the lineage outside the schema @ :2:45
-- out/third-root/bind --
verdict: E0141
E0141 n in schema 0.0 refers to name, which is declared in the lineage outside the schema @ :2:45
-- out/together/bind --
verdict: E0141
E0141 n in schema 0.0 refers to name, which is declared in the lineage outside the schema @ /m/text.cue:3:45
-- out/unify-text-use/bind --
verdict: E0141
E0141 joinSchema refers to #J, which is declared in the lineage outside the joinSchema @ /m/in.cue:5:49
E0141 n in schema 0.0 refers to name, which is declared in the lineage outside the schema @ :2:45
-- out/unify-use-text/bind --
verdict: E0141
E0141 n in schema 0.0 refers to name, which is declared in the lineage outside the schema @ :2:45
